#
# Here's the introduction
#
[scene#D]

[cue#1]
4;moveto %s;query_Omas_location
4;expressions: interrupt *>[say] Oma, found another case of wine... Burgundy, I'd guess.
10;cue oma D2
[end_cue]

[cue#3]
4;expressions: nod
4;cue oma D4
[end_cue]

[cue#5]
6;*>[say] Well, lets see...
8;expressions: read *>[say] Contents: Yliastrum Elixir - a life extension plasma.  Uses: Life extension, instantaneous muscle and stamina building.
12;cue Grandfeathers D6
[end_cue]

[cue#A]
6;*>[say] Well it does say: 'Warning: The effect of overdoses remains unstudied.'
6;expressions: read *>[say] It goes on,'The contents herein presented to the special conference of Medical Academia of Europe. It's signed Vividus, Paracelsus.
14;cue Oma DB
[end_cue]

[cue#C]
6;*>[say] Well, if you'll just follow me.
8;move west
10;*>[say] Everyone coming? Great.
16;*>[say] This Chateau is thought to be originally built upon the site of a structure built by the Babenberg family, around 1100... This way folks.
16;move west
16;*>[say] at least thats what they figure from the stonework found in the cellar and here in the towers.
10;*>[say] Careful up the stairs here, they're rather steep.
8;move up
14;*>[say] Later it fell into the hands of the Bohemians, who shortly there after lost it in a war with the Hapsburg family. The Hapsburgs owned all of Austria right up until the first World War.
14;*>[say] This way...
4;move south
10;*>[say] During the early Hapsburg rule it was built upon for the marriage of a Hapsburg daughters. However, she chose instead to elope with a peasant, and the place stood gathering dust for many, many years.
16;*>[say] Then in 1540, Paracelsus, the great physician, was called upon by Prince Ernst of Bavaria for a special cure. Paracelsus successfully cured the desperate Ernst and was rewarded by both a promise of support for his research, as well as a bride, Ernst niece of Hapsburgian descent, Carmilla Karnstein.
16;look busts *>[say] In fact this room, and particularly this bust was created in honor of the Princes kindness.
16;*>[say] Over in this section of the gallery...
8;move east
12;*>[say] ...you can see various Karnstein family members as well as Paracelsus himself.
12;expressions: smile *>[say] Hey, I'm remembering this pretty good... my grandparents and I have only been here for a few months, and it's taken me a while but I'm finally getting this part memorized!
12;move east
12;*>[say] And here, you see the last owner before we were awarded federal funding to restore this chateau. Mircalla Karnstein, shown here in this portrait, apparently committed suicide. A great sorrow befell the once great Karnstein family, that later died out.
12;expressions: laugh *>[say] Some rumors had it that the schloss was haunted by Mircalla, other rumors I heard from kids at school say a pack of blood thirsty gypsies had moved into the place, stealing and eating the towns children.
1;expressions: smile
12;*>[say] Well, that's about all I can remember... right this way to your rooms.
8;move south
12;*>[say] Now, if you'll just glance at the room key Oma gave you, you'll find your room number, with rooms 1 through 6 are here on the western side of the chateau, and 7 through 13, are here on the eastern side.
12;expressions: smile *>[say] We hope you enjoy your stay here at the Karnstein Chateau.
4;moveto +4+6+0
[end_cue]
[end_scene]
